The server strips the manifest's advisory `notes` before serving
/api/v1/settings/contract. The tests below use the contract fields rather than
those notes.

The runner reads the manifest for the facts the generated bindings in
iosApp/iosApp/Networking/SettingKeys.generated.swift do not carry:
resolution_order, default_value, value_schema.ordered plus its enum member
order, and constrained_by. Those are what the fixture's expectations actually
test, so the resolver in Tests/SettingsContractResolve.swift is driven by the
contract rather than by a hand-copied table.
